: "toolu_01BThaRqCJF17CKW9ac3hwCg", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0 (all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west) left the service degraded with an 18% error rate. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; the rollback is confirmed in all regions. Root cause of the v5.1.0 regression needs investigation.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19230, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BThaRqCJF17CKW9ac3hwCg", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19230, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BThaRqCJF17CKW9ac3hwCg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19230, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011GJGe1aJMfPxgGe3CfJMfK", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19530, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011GJGe1aJMfPxgGe3CfJMfK", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19530, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011GJGe1aJMfPxgGe3CfJMfK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25936, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2 incident. Errors are back down to normal levels.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called `payments`, so I tried a few likely names. The affected one is **`payments-api`**. This morning's v5.1.0 release was marked degraded, and the service was failing 18% of requests in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west).\n- **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to **v5.0.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production. This didn't need change-manager approval, because the policy only covers versions that have never been healthy in production. The rollback is confirmed in all three regions, and the service now shows as healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, `payments-api`), which paged on-call. It records the v5.1.0 failure, the rollback to v5.0.0 and that the cause still needs investigating.\n\nI found the service by guessing names, so there could be other payments services I didn't check. If another one was also part of this morning's deploy, tell me its name and I'll look at it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013kM1o9zjJcDtyQn9A8qmKT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SP8hK5MhHDX5RnRDpBy7hV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R5ky37LqMoa6KohSYazZSR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013KstuhapvXajRhjbCxVEjV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LanuNgjcwUgeEe4ApX178P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CXQ8YtFBWY4oZknvLkTnjX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payment-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WsoEJvrYFnuuXRZasGD8Zj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019Y9d7Sx1KD5KvjLiWtxXq3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "version": "v5.0.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BThaRqCJF17CKW9ac3hwCg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0 (all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west) left the service degraded with an 18% error rate. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; the rollback is confirmed in all regions. Root cause of the v5.1.0 regression needs investigation.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011GJGe1aJMfPxgGe3CfJMfK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2 incident. Errors are back down to normal levels.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called `payments`, so I tried a few likely names. The affected one is **`payments-api`**. This morning's v5.1.0 release was marked degraded, and the service was failing 18% of requests in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west).\n- **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to **v5.0.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production. This didn't need change-manager approval, because the policy only covers versions that have never been healthy in production. The rollback is confirmed in all three regions, and the service now shows as healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, `payments-api`), which paged on-call. It records the v5.1.0 failure, the rollback to v5.0.0 and that the cause still needs investigating.\n\nI found the service by guessing names, so there could be other payments services I didn't check. If another one was also part of this morning's deploy, tell me its name and I'll look at it.", "type": "text"}]}]}